@startuml reservation-flow-sequence
!pragma teoz true
title Reservation creation — HTTP, idempotency, transaction and outbox
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam wrapWidth 350
autonumber

actor Client
participant "Symfony HTTP /\nReservationController" as HTTP
participant ReservationService as Service
participant ReservationRepository as Repo
participant "Doctrine\nEntityManager" as EM
participant OutboxRecorder as Outbox
database "PostgreSQL\nbooking" as DB
participant OutboxRelayCommand as Relay
participant "Messenger event.bus\nAMQP outbound transport" as Bus
queue "RabbitMQ\nticketing exchange" as MQ

    note over HTTP,Outbox: Booking uses an application service, not a CreateReservation command/handler.\nReservation is the persisted model, no separate domain service is called.
    Client -> HTTP: POST /api/reservations\nJSON + Idempotency-Key
    HTTP -> HTTP: MapRequestPayload → CreateReservationRequest\ndeserialize + validate
    break Invalid payload or missing/empty Idempotency-Key
        HTTP --> Client: HTTP error (validation: 422, missing key: 400)
    end
    HTTP -> Service: create(payload, idempotencyKey)
    Service -> Repo: findByIdempotencyKey(key)
    Repo -> DB: SELECT reservations by idempotency_key
    DB --> Repo: Reservation or null
    Repo --> Service: Existing reservation or null
    break Existing reservation
        Service -> Service: resolveDuplicate() → payloadMatches()
        note right of Service: Compare showId, normalized seatIds,\nbuyerName and buyerEmail.
        alt Same payload
            Service -> Service: ReservationMapper::toResponse(existing)
            Service --> HTTP: ReservationResponse (current stored status)
            HTTP --> Client: 202 Accepted (same reservationId)
        else Different payload
            Service --> HTTP: IdempotencyPayloadMismatchException
            HTTP --> Client: 409 Conflict (framework.yaml mapping)
        end
    end

group Local creation transaction
        note over Service,DB: Local atomic transaction — EntityManager::wrapInTransaction()
        Service -> EM: wrapInTransaction(callback)
        EM -> DB: BEGIN
        Service -> Repo: findByIdempotencyKey(key) — race recheck
        Repo -> DB: SELECT reservations by idempotency_key
        DB --> Repo: Reservation or null
        Repo --> Service: Race-check result
        note over Service,EM: If found: resolveDuplicate() as above, no new writes.\nMatching result commits, payload mismatch rolls back → 409.
        opt Still no reservation for this key
            Service -> Service: new Reservation(UUIDv7 id, UUIDv7 correlationId, ...)
            note right of Service: Initial status PENDING,\nconstructor deduplicates seatIds.\nNo availability check or payment here.
            Service -> EM: persist(reservation)
            Service -> Outbox: record(new ReservationRequested(...),\nreservationId, correlationId)
            Outbox -> Outbox: Serialize event, resolve reservation.requested\nnew OutboxMessage(UUIDv7, payload, metadata)
            Outbox -> EM: persist(outboxMessage)
            Service -> Service: ReservationMapper::toResponse(reservation)
        end
        note over Service,EM: Callback produces DTO before flush, create() returns only after commit.
        EM -> DB: flush() — INSERT reservations + outbox_messages (if new)
        alt Successful transaction
            EM -> DB: COMMIT
            EM --> Service: ReservationResponse
        else Transaction failure
            EM -> EM: close()
            EM -> DB: ROLLBACK
            note over EM,DB: Neither new row is committed.
            EM --> Service: Exception
        end
    end
    break Transaction failed
        alt UniqueConstraintViolationException (concurrent insert)
            Service -> EM: clear()
            Service -> Repo: findByIdempotencyKey(key)
            Repo -> DB: Reload winning reservation
            DB --> Repo: Reservation or null
            Repo --> Service: Reload result
            note over Service,HTTP: Existing → resolveDuplicate(): matching payload → 202, mismatch → 409.\nMissing → RuntimeException. This is the implemented catch path,\nit does not reset the EntityManager closed by Doctrine.
        else Other exception
            Service --> HTTP: Propagate exception
            HTTP --> Client: Error response (no successful creation)
        end
    end
    Service --> HTTP: ReservationResponse
    HTTP --> Client: 202 Accepted (PENDING for a new reservation)


== Separate outbox relay process ==
    note over DB,MQ: Separate relay process, only committed rows are visible.\nMay run before or after HTTP response delivery, HTTP does not wait for the saga.
    Relay -> DB: OutboxMessageRepository::findUnpublished(limit)\npublished_at IS NULL, oldest first
    DB --> Relay: OutboxMessage[]
    loop Each unpublished row
        Relay -> Relay: Deserialize payload to ReservationRequested
        Relay -> Bus: dispatch(event, AmqpStamp)\nrouting key + message_id=outbox.id + correlation_id
        Bus -> MQ: Publish reservation.requested → orchestrator.queue
        Bus --> Relay: dispatch() returns
        Relay -> Relay: OutboxMessage::markPublished() (in memory)
    end
    Relay -> EM: flush() after the entire batch
    EM -> DB: UPDATE outbox_messages.published_at
    note over Relay,MQ: Publish and marking are not atomic: failure before final flush can republish.\nSame outbox row retains message_id (at-least-once delivery).
    note right of MQ: Async continuation in orchestrator-service:\nReservationRequestedHandler::__invoke()\n→ SagaCoordinator::handle()\n→ ReservationRequestedStrategy::handle().\nSeat holding and payment belong to the subsequent saga.
@enduml
